+# Live competitor data
+
+Seven categories now take their competitor layer from real data instead of the simulator:
+**grocery, pharmacy, qsr, cafe, fuel, bank, ev**. Every other category stays simulated and is labelled as such.
+
+| Category | Feasibility | Map source (OSM tags) | Registry for offline businesses |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Fuel station | **89%** | `amenity=fuel` | PESO licences, IOCL/BPCL/HPCL outlet locators |
+| Banking & NBFC | **86%** | `amenity=bank` | RBI branch master / IFSC list |
+| QSR & fast food | **72%** | `amenity=fast_food` | FSSAI FoSCoS |
+| Pharmacy | **70%** | `amenity=pharmacy`, `shop=chemist` | FDA Maharashtra drug licences |
+| Cafe & coffee | **67%** | `amenity=cafe` | FSSAI FoSCoS |
+| Supermarket & grocery | **64%** | `shop=supermarket|grocery`, food wholesale | FSSAI FoSCoS |
+| EV charging | **62%** | `amenity=charging_station` | BEE list, Tata Power EZ / Statiq / ChargeZone |
+
+Feasibility = 40% map coverage + 25% registry quality + 20% freshness + 15% brand signal (assessed estimates, `server/src/data/liveSources.js`).
+
+## How it flows
+1. `startScheduler()` runs 15 s after boot, then every `LIVE_REFRESH_HOURS` (default 12). `LIVE_DATA=off` disables it.
+2. `syncCategory()` pulls Overpass, filters to the Pune & PCMC polygon, merges `server/data/registry/<key>.csv`, dedupes within 60 m.
+3. New outlets are added; map outlets missing from the latest pull become `closed / NOT_IN_LATEST_OSM`; cancelled licences become `closed / REGISTRY_CANCELLED`; outlets that come back are reopened.
+4. Simulated POIs of that category are deleted only after a successful live pull. A failed or empty pull keeps the old data.
+5. `reloadEverywhere()` reloads Node state, clears catchment + response caches and calls `POST /ml/reload` on the Python service, so hexagons, scores, recommendations, stress tests, portfolio and cannibalisation all recompute.
+
+## What-if: "this competitor doesn't exist"
+Competitor modal → **What if this competitor doesn't exist?** → `POST /api/live/competitors/:id/status {status:"closed"}`.
+The whole app recomputes. Restore from Trust Center → Real-time data feasibility → Removed competitors.
+What-if closures are global (shared by all users) and are never reopened by the scheduler.
+
+## API
+* `GET  /api/live/status[?category=]`: feasibility, source mix, last sync, closures
+* `POST /api/live/refresh[?category=]`: sync now (login)
+* `POST /api/live/registry/:category` `{rows:[{name,lat,lon,regNo,status}]}`: merge registry rows (login)
+* `POST /api/live/competitors/:id/status` `{status:"open"|"closed", reason}`: what-if (login)
+* `GET  /api/live/competitors/closed[?category=]`
+
+## Does the model need retraining?
+* **Placeholder engine (what Render runs today, no `ML_SERVICE_URL`)**: no. It scores competition relative to the city median (`compRef`), so it adapts to real counts automatically.
+* **Python RandomForest (`backend/`)**: trained on 357 rows of *simulated* competitor counts and *simulated* revenue (spatial-CV R² 0.14).
+  Real OSM layers are several times denser, so raw counts would fall outside the training range, where a forest just
+  returns its edge leaf. A **drift guard** (`competitor_scale`, `LIVE_DRIFT_GUARD=on`) rescales live counts to the training
+  density so the model sees relative intensity. Retraining on live features only makes sense once there is **real revenue**
+  (own-store uploads / outcomes); retraining on the simulator's revenue would just re-learn the simulator.
